    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="1079" n="965" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg965"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The only source found for this conversation is the following informal note by
                    Harriman: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Had a talk with Eden about Russia and the proposed discussion, and the
                                agenda.”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d424-f1"/> (Harriman Papers)</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d424-f1" n="1" xml:id="d424-f1-content">
                <p>The reference is apparently to the proposed tripartite meeting at the Foreign
                    Ministers level. For further background on this conference, which was convened
                    at Moscow in October 1943, see <ref target="frus1943v01#pg_513">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 513</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
